Day 39/120 – Data Modelling

Today was all about data modelling.

Data modelling is the process of organizing and structuring data to create meaningful relationships between different tables. It helps ensure that data flows correctly and can be analyzed efficiently.

I learned how to:
	•	Understand relationships between tables
	•	Define primary and foreign keys
	•	Build structured models for better analysis
	•	Improve data consistency and accuracy

Data modelling is a crucial step because a well-structured model makes analysis smoother, faster, and more reliable.
